  "title": "Calorie estimates: remaining count units (head, bunch, \"N g each\", bare can)",
  "description": "Progress 2026-10-02: curated entries and SR food_overrides can now carry cited piece weights (see the catalog README), and the first batch landed (corn tortilla sizes, anchovy, ear of corn, bacon slice, garlic head, parsnip, ham and prosciutto slices, lettuce leaf and head, baguette, hamburger and hot dog buns, lasagna noodles, nori sheets); pipeline-fixture lines with Unsupported quantity unit went from 874 to 701, prod (owner) from 151 to 114. \
Then a hand-maintained bespoke.json added referenced weights no database gives (shallot sizes, poblano, inch pieces of ginger, herb, scallion, kale and asparagus bunches, broccoli heads, yeast packets, squash) and standard US can sizes for a bare can (owner decision); pipeline lines went to 426, prod to 92. \
Progress 2026-10-05: \"zest/juice of <count> <citrus>\" lines now parse with the fruit as the unit (\"1 lemon\" of lemon juice), and bespoke.json carries per-fruit juice (USDA \"lemon yields\" and the like) and zest weights for lemon, lime and orange; grams_per_piece also reads a sized piece with no exact portion (\"large lemon\") as the piece. \
Meyer lemon, key lime, grapefruit, clementine and tangerine units still have no weight. \
Progress 2026-10-10: a per-item weight next to a count (\"2 cans, 10 oz each\") now weighs the count times it; pipeline lines went from 465 to 452. \
Progress 2026-10-12: dash, pinch and drop of a food that isn't a trace spice (hot sauce, Worcestershire, a pinch of sugar) weigh as 1/8, 1/16 and 1/96 tsp with the food's density, and \"packed cup\" / \"packed tsp\" weigh as plain volumes (as \"1 cup packed\" already did; brown sugar's density is the packed cup); pipeline lines went from 314 to 289. \
Remaining groups in the pipeline fixtures (2026-10-12 dump): bare counts with the unit left in the item (\"envelope active dry yeast\", \"loaf french bread\", \"ball pizza dough\", \"sleeve saltine crackers\", \"strips lemon zest\": parser changes), size words alone (\"1 large savoy cabbage\", \"1 medium kohlrabi\", \"small butternut squash\"), \"piece\" (ginger, bread, bacon), handfuls, \"750-ml bottle\" of wine, and \"8-ounce wheel\" of brie. \
Still open: crushed tomatoes' bare can (two common sizes), and the long tail in the audit's Unsupported quantity unit list. \
After count units landed, about 740 pipeline-fixture lines (1.2%) still fail with Unsupported quantity unit. \
USDA SR Legacy has no per-piece weight for these, so each needs a cited curated value or a parser change rather than an import rule. \
Largest groups: (1) \"head\" (garlic, lettuce, cauliflower) and \"bunch\" (herbs, kale, scallions): add curated per-piece weights with a source. (3) A bare \"can\" / \"package\" with no stated weight: probably stays unknown, but a standard 15-ounce can for beans and tomatoes is worth an owner decision. (4) \"inch piece\" of ginger and \"handful\". \
Run make ingredient-catalog-audit to measure before and after.",
